   579→        when: kspec serve --daemon executed
   580→        then: starts in background, writes PID file, returns immediately with status message
   581→      - id: ac-3
   582→        given: daemon not running
   583→        when: kspec serve --port 8080 executed
   584→        then: starts on specified port
   585→      - id: ac-4
   586→        given: daemon running
   587→        when: kspec serve stop executed
   588→        then: sends SIGTERM to daemon PID, waits for clean shutdown, removes PID file
   589→      - id: ac-5
   590→        given: daemon not running
   591→        when: kspec serve stop executed
   592→        then: outputs 'Daemon not running' with exit code 0 (idempotent)
   593→      - id: ac-6
   594→        given: any state
   595→        when: kspec serve status executed
   596→        then: outputs JSON with {running, pid, port, uptime, connections}
   597→      - id: ac-7
   598→        given: daemon running
   599→        when: kspec serve restart executed
   600→        then: stops existing daemon, starts new one, preserves port setting
   601→      - id: ac-8
   602→        given: any state
   603→        when: kspec serve logs executed
   604→        then: tails daemon log file (.kspec/.daemon.log)
   605→      - id: ac-9
   606→        given: daemon running
   607→        when: kspec serve logs --follow executed
   608→        then: streams log output continuously until Ctrl+C
   609→      - id: ac-10
   610→        given: port already in use
   611→        when: kspec serve attempts to start
   612→        then: fails with clear error message suggesting --port flag
